From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:29:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 41/41] hottyterm: stage stamps for the latency rig
 (HOTTY_TRACE)

With HOTTY_TRACE=<dir>, the terminal writes hottyterm-<pid>.jsonl in the
trace format hotty/1 (hottyterm's docs/trace.md): one line per stage on
the shared monotonic clock. The stages are the key and pointer events,
the pty's reads and writes, each parsed batch and hotty command,
hotty-blitz's rendering, the renderer's draw and upload, and GTK taking
the frame. Off, a stamp is one atomic load and a branch.

The writer is in hotty.zig. Upstream files get 17 lines of hooks:
Surface.zig 4, termio/Exec.zig 6, renderer/generic.zig 5,
apprt/gtk/class/render_surface.zig 2.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
